  notes:[B('The course says Eysenck found “two major differences which could be measured” but does not name them. They are introversion–extroversion and stability–instability (neuroticism).','Di course talk say Eysenck see “two major difference wey you fit measure” but e no name dem. Na introvert–extrovert and stable–unstable (neuroticism).'),B('The printed 16PF table is misaligned: several “low score” labels appear one row off. The idea to learn is that each factor runs between two poles.','Di 16PF table wey dem print scatter: some “low score” label dey one row off. Wetin to learn na say each factor get two end.'),B('“Karen Homey” should read Karen Horney.','“Karen Homey” suppose be Karen Horney.')],
